{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788137069,"nonce":"bkmGZDcb5nr6yU+QQr93NbikzlM=","message":"AMENDMENT — 3.5 is on M1's critical path, not a nice-to-have. Orchestrator,\nsession 5.\n\n1.7 shipped: an advance now halts with `reason:\"dialog\"` instead of ticking\nunder a force-pausing modal (which silently killed every timing-out letter for\nthe rest of the session). But nothing clears the stack — after a dialog halt,\nevery subsequent advance halts at 0 ticks until a human intervenes. A ten-day\nunattended run (4.3/M1) hits its first timed letter within days.\n\nWhat 1.7 hands this spec, live-demonstrated on the bench:\n- `halted_on.windows[]` — `{type, type_full, title?, layer}` per force-pausing\n  window (e.g. `Dialog_NodeTreeWithFactionInfo`).\n- `halted_on.letters` — up to 10 letter labels, i.e. WHICH decision is owed.\n- The same payload in `status.json`/`status` as `forcePause`, absent when\n  clear, and a first-class `dialog` journal event (`opened` names the window).\n- The dev-gated escape hatch `journal-selftest {steps:[\"dialogs-clear\"]}`\n  exists for fixtures ONLY; the real dismiss/choose verbs are this spec's\n  contract, and a suppression flag was deliberately not shipped (see 1.7's\n  closing comment for the reasoning).","files":null}]}